xnu 0516: bound the GPT entry table before multiplying

ufs_find_partition() read the GPT header's entry count and size from the disk
and rejected a table whose byte count did not fit BOUNCE_SIZE. The product was
computed in 32 bits, so a corrupt header with a large enough entry count wrapped
and passed the check; ufs_read_blocks() was then asked for a bogus block count
and the read walked off the bounce buffer. Compare the count against
BOUNCE_SIZE / esz instead, which cannot wrap. esz is checked to be 128 first,
so the division is safe.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
index 86b904f..e85c25f 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -548,7 +548,7 @@ ufs_find_partition(const char *want)
 	memcpy(&entry_lba, b + 72, 8);
 	memcpy(&nent, b + 80, 4);
 	memcpy(&esz, b + 84, 4);
-	if (esz != 128 || nent == 0 || nent * esz > BOUNCE_SIZE) {
+	if (esz != 128 || nent == 0 || nent > BOUNCE_SIZE / esz) {
 		printf("MONDRIAN UFS: unsupported GPT entries %u x %u\n", nent, esz);
 		UFS_WHY("unsupported GPT entries %u x %u", nent, esz);
 		return ENXIO;
